                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "What wore me down was everything around it: no tutorial whatsoever, a camera locked to 90 degree turns, and a blur filter I could never switch off that had my eyes aching by the second session. Combat is the real problem though, since every single attack is a timing prompt that whiffs more often than it should, and running dry on stamina means burning turns on defend just to attack again. By my third run chasing objectives I was doing the same bunny hunting and chest scavenging on the same flat maps, and then a final boss with randomly rolled stats one shot my fully geared party. There is a good little game buried in here and the dev clearly cared, but I can't tell anyone to pay full price for it.",
